    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0147" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) Regulations/9881: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-25T15:00:00-04:00">February 25, 1943—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>394. Referring to Henry’s telephone conversation of February 17 with
                        Ravndal<anchor n="34" xml:id="d129-f1"/> arrangements completed for
                    establishment of decentralized export control in Bolivia effective April 1.
                    Henry and Wilkinson<anchor n="35" xml:id="d129-f2"/> leaving for Santiago on the
                    first available airplane.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d129-f1" n="34" xml:id="d129-f1-content">
                <p>Christian M. Ravndal, Chief of the Division of Exports and Requirements of the
                    Department.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d129-f2" n="35" xml:id="d129-f2-content">
                <p>Horton Henry of the Department and H. A. Wilkinson of the Board of Economic
                    Warfare were assigned to present a modified plan of decentralized export control
                    in certain of the American Republics.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
